& [Observed] is exact
  + stable agent identity contains mutable purpose, program, authority, and lifecycle state
  + stable environment identity contains mutable adapter and instance-description revisions
  + session identity and immutable cursors contain mutable lifecycle or disposition state
  + normal transitions would therefore make one durable identity resolve to incompatible content

& [RootCause] is conceptual, logical, and physical identity collapse
  + natural keys were combined with versioned definitions and mutable snapshots in the first verbose source
  + the desire for compact complete records displaced the required separation of identity, revision, and lifecycle transition

& [EffectAccount] is zero
  + the defect was found before explosion, canonical specification, satisfaction signature, implementation, test, or execution
  + no Minecraft server, game world, model, runtime process, dependency, or Cantor code changed

& [Correction] is governed
  + preserve the original source and manifest byte-exactly
  + preserve a separate corrective source and revision manifest
  + represent stable keys, immutable revisions, and ordered snapshots as distinct records
  + re-audit both source snapshots before SJS proceeds
  - never: edit the base source to hide the defect
  - never: let a collision fault substitute for a coherent identity model

& [ReusableGuardrail] is lifecycle identity review
  + every field on a stable identity must remain true for the entire identity lifetime
  + mutable configuration, authority, cursor, lifecycle, and observation fields belong in versioned records or snapshots
  + a content digest identifies immutable content and does not replace a stable natural key when continuity across revisions matters
